keywords:
  - neuromorphic photonics
  - diffractive neural network
  - slow light
  - Kerr nonlinearity
  - optical ROM
  - bound state in the continuum
  - GaN
abstract: >
  Concept paper proposing OLLMU, a hybrid optical inference architecture
  that stores frozen model weights in a three-dimensional diffractive core
  and routes selected fields into slow-light side loops for delay memory
  and Kerr-type nonlinearity. The GaN quasi-BIC blue laser is treated as a
  candidate coherent source, not as a working optical LLM. Claims are
  labelled Fact, Literature, Hypothesis, or Estimate. Implementation is
  unrestricted; originator attribution (Anisul Wałsymzerp) must be kept.
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-09-07"
